IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999: WHICH TEXT IS DEPOSITED, and what the deposit's own markers say about the text on other dates.
--
-- THE DEPOSIT.  registers/source-bundle/TA1999.txt is the Singapore Statutes Online consolidation headed "Informal
-- Consolidation - version in force from 2/10/2026" (2020 Revised Edition).  TA1999.meta.json says it was retrieved on
-- 2026-10-09, "Current version as at 09 Oct 2026", and its historical_versions list ends at 20251001, so the list is one
-- version behind the text (the text carries an amendment marked "[Act 13 of 2026 wef 02/10/2026]" at s 97(2)(ga)).
-- No earlier version of the Act is deposited: Singapore Statutes Online refuses automated requests, and lawplain serves one
-- version only.  So:
--   * the STRICT function below says the deposited text is the text in force from 2 October 2026 and nothing earlier;
--   * the INFERENCE function reads the deposit's own margin markers ("[10/2005]", "[30/2016]" and so on) to say whether the
--     deposited WORDING of a section can have been in force on an earlier date.  It is an inference from markers, not a text.
--     It is kept apart from the strict function so that no answer is ever drawn from it silently.
-- The markers show amendments since the 2000 Revised Edition (operation 30 December 2000).  A section with no marker has the
-- wording it had then.  A marker names an Act; the Act's commencement date comes from the Legislative History at the end of the
-- deposit (TA1999.txt:7107 onwards): Act 10 of 2005 began 16 February 2005 (except ss 10 and 11), Act 19 of 2011 on 1 February 2012,
-- Act 22 of 2016 on 1 October 2016, Act 30 of 2016 on 1 February 2017, Act 4 of 2021 on 1 March 2021, Act 25 of 2021 on 1 April 2022.

§ `The deposited text and the SSO versions`

-- The versions the deposit's meta.json lists (SSO "historical versions"), plus the 2 October 2026 version from the text's banner.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`TA: the start of the SSO version in force on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d AT LEAST (Date 2 10 2026) THEN JUST (Date 2 10 2026)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 1 10 2025) THEN JUST (Date 1 10 2025)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 1 11 2022) THEN JUST (Date 1 11 2022)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 1 4 2022) THEN JUST (Date 1 4 2022)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 13 1 2022) THEN JUST (Date 13 1 2022)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 31 12 2021) THEN JUST (Date 31 12 2021)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 1 3 2021) THEN JUST (Date 1 3 2021)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 30 7 2020) THEN JUST (Date 30 7 2020)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2020) THEN JUST (Date 1 1 2020)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 16 5 2018) THEN JUST (Date 16 5 2018)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 23 5 2017) THEN JUST (Date 23 5 2017)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 1 2 2017) THEN JUST (Date 1 2 2017)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 1 10 2016) THEN JUST (Date 1 10 2016)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 1 2 2012) THEN JUST (Date 1 2 2012)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 16 2 2005) THEN JUST (Date 16 2 2005)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 30 12 2000) THEN JUST (Date 30 12 2000)
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 1 12 1999) THEN JUST (Date 1 12 1999)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- STRICT: the deposited text speaks for the dates from 2 October 2026.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`TA: the deposited consolidation is the text in force on the date` MEANS d AT LEAST (Date 2 10 2026)

§ `What the deposit's own markers say about a section's wording`

-- The last amendment marked on each Tier 1 section, by section number as the 2020 Revised Edition prints it.
-- (Markers read from TA1999.txt: s 2 at 289, 378, 469, 546, 550 and 556 (Act 12 of 2020 wef 1 October 2025 on two definitions, S 26/2022 wef 13 January 2022 on three, and the closing list 10/2005, 19/2011, 22/2016, 30/2016, 4/2021); s 5 at 653-711; s 11 at 1193-1238; s 53 at 4839-4886; s 84 at 5932; s 85 at 5952;
-- s 95 at 6996.  Sections 3, 4, 54 to 59, 64, 71, 86 to 88, 96 and 98 carry only the 2000 Edition number marker.)
GIVEN section IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Marker history`
`TA markers: the last marked amendment of the section` MEANS
    BRANCH IF section EQUALS "2" THEN JUST (`last marked amendment began on` OF 1, 10, 2025)
           IF section EQUALS "5" THEN JUST (`last marked amendment began on` OF 1, 2, 2017)
           IF section EQUALS "11" THEN JUST (`last marked amendment began on` OF 1, 2, 2012)
           IF section EQUALS "53" THEN JUST (`last marked amendment began on` OF 1, 4, 2022)
           IF section EQUALS "84" THEN JUST (`last marked amendment began on` OF 16, 2, 2005)
           IF section EQUALS "85" THEN JUST (`last marked amendment began on` OF 16, 2, 2005)
           IF section EQUALS "95" THEN JUST (`last marked amendment began on` OF 16, 2, 2005)
           IF section EQUALS "3" OR section EQUALS "4" OR section EQUALS "54" OR section EQUALS "55" OR section EQUALS "56" THEN JUST `no amendment marker after the 2000 Revised Edition`
           IF section EQUALS "57" OR section EQUALS "58" OR section EQUALS "59" OR section EQUALS "64" OR section EQUALS "71" THEN JUST `no amendment marker after the 2000 Revised Edition`
           IF section EQUALS "86" OR section EQUALS "87" OR section EQUALS "88" OR section EQUALS "96" OR section EQUALS "98" THEN JUST `no amendment marker after the 2000 Revised Edition`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- INFERENCE (not a text): the deposited wording of the section can have been in force on the date, because no marked
-- amendment began after the date and the date is not before the 2000 Revised Edition.  NOTHING when the markers do not speak.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      section IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`TA markers: on the markers, the deposited wording of the section was in force on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 30 12 2000) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `TA markers: the last marked amendment of the section` section
               WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
               WHEN JUST h THEN
                   CONSIDER h
                   WHEN `no amendment marker after the 2000 Revised Edition` THEN JUST TRUE
                   WHEN `last marked amendment began on` day month year THEN JUST (d AT LEAST (Date day month year))

§ `Per-term markers of section 2 (read from the amending Bills, as introduced)`

-- The marker at the end of s 2 is one closing list for the whole section, so it cannot say which definition a given Act touched.  The Bills can, when
-- they are read, so this function records what they say, for the definitions that other modules of this encoding use.  Read on 2026-11-04 through the
-- lawplain `bills` corpus (not deposited here): Bill 67/2004 (Act 10 of 2005), clause 2; Bill 20/2011 (Act 19 of 2011), clause 2; Bill 30/2016
-- (Act 30 of 2016), clause 2.  Each is the Bill AS INTRODUCED.  The Act's Legislative History lists, for each of the three, one date for the
-- Second and Third Readings and no Notice of Amendments (TA1999.txt:7134-7143, 7145-7151, 7171-7178; it does list Notices of Amendments for other
-- Acts, at 7121, 7201 and 7216), so the Bill is taken to be the text enacted; that is an inference from the history, not a read of the Act.
-- Read since, on 2026-11-04, from the e-Gazette's printed Acts (deposited): Act 30 of 2016 (TA1999.ACT30-2016.txt) sections 1 to 20 are word for word clauses 1 to 20 of the Bill 30/2016 as introduced
-- (compared by script, word sequences, ratio 1.0), which confirms the inference above for that Act; and section 100 of the Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016
-- (Act 22 of 2016, TA1999.ACT22-2016.txt) amends s 2 by replacing the definition of "Authority" and of "Chief Executive" and deleting that of "Media Development Authority of
-- Singapore", none of the terms below.  Both Acts are now versions in sgta-ta-versions.l4.
-- Act 15 of 2017 (the Companies (Amendment) Act 2017, TA1999.ACT15-2017.txt, deposited 2026-11-04) amends the Telecommunications Act only by its section 53(6), which inserts "or 211I" in ss 32J(3)(a) and 32L(1)(b) and (2)(a)
-- (TA1999.ACT15-2017.txt:4217-4219); it touches s 2 not at all, and it is a version in sgta-ta-versions.l4 as well.
-- STILL NOT read, so a date these could change is not covered: the s 2 amendments of the Statute Law Reform Act 2021 (Act 4 of 2021; history line 7236-7245 says its
-- amendments were made by its section 22(9), and Bill 45/2020 as introduced has only 11 clauses and none on this Act), and of the other Acts the history lists after Act 15 of 2017 (NOTES.md, "Acts and instruments whose source was not obtained").
--   * "broadcasting apparatus" and "broadcasting service": inserted by Act 10 of 2005, from 16 February 2005.
--   * "equipment" and "telecommunication system": amended by Act 19 of 2011, from 1 February 2012.  Before that date "equipment" read "... used or intended
--     to be used for telecommunication purposes" and "telecommunication system" had no words about broadcasting (Bill 20/2011, clause 2(b) and (e)).
--   * "telecommunication service": ", including the leasing of a telecommunication cable," added by Act 30 of 2016, from 1 February 2017.
--   * "telecommunications", "radio-communication", "Hertzian or radio waves", "message", "radio-communication service" and "radio-communication system":
--     named by none of the three Bills, so on those Bills the deposited wording is the 2000 Revised Edition wording (30 December 2000).
GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`TA s 2 per-term markers: the date from which the deposited wording of the definition was in force, on the 2004, 2011 and 2016 Bills` MEANS
    BRANCH IF term EQUALS "equipment" OR term EQUALS "telecommunication system" THEN JUST (Date 1 2 2012)
           IF term EQUALS "broadcasting apparatus" OR term EQUALS "broadcasting service" THEN JUST (Date 16 2 2005)
           IF term EQUALS "telecommunication service" THEN JUST (Date 1 2 2017)
           IF term EQUALS "telecommunications" OR term EQUALS "radio-communication" OR term EQUALS "Hertzian or radio waves" THEN JUST (Date 30 12 2000)
           IF term EQUALS "message" OR term EQUALS "radio-communication service" OR term EQUALS "radio-communication system" THEN JUST (Date 30 12 2000)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- INFERENCE (not a text): the deposited wording of the s 2 definition was in force on the date, on the three Bills above.
-- NOTHING when the term is not one of those recorded, and for a date before the 2000 Revised Edition.  FALSE when a later Act changed it.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`TA s 2 per-term markers: the deposited wording of the definition was in force on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 30 12 2000) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `TA s 2 per-term markers: the date from which the deposited wording of the definition was in force, on the 2004, 2011 and 2016 Bills` term
               WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
               WHEN JUST from THEN JUST (d AT LEAST from)
